  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Socio-Economic Empowerment of Women Home-based Workers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project places direct attention on improving gender equality and women&#x2019;s human rights through economic empowerment, as the project focusses on women workers in the informal and formal sectors of the economy. The change factor will have a direct impact on 11,500 women beneficiaries through the proposed interventions and will indirectly benefit household members including men, boys and communities at large. The proposed project will lead to increased voice and visibility of WHBWs, women entrepreneurs, women-owned businesses and women formal sector women workers. The project displays a deep understanding of the socio-cultural context and policy environment with respect to WEE, gender equality barriers including access to resources and opportunities, and gender based violence (GBV). There is a particular focus on zero tolerance to GBV, age and disability violence.It will deliver special trainings on inclusion, access and intersectionality of age, gender and disability for all beneficiaries and implementing partners.</narrative>
  </description>
